  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Community Stabilization in Wider Lake Chad Basin</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The stability in the frontier provinces of Chad is often at risk, with the socio-economic and security conditions being extremely precarious. While the Lac province in the wider Lake Chad region is often in the limelight, receiving consistent attention from humanitarian and development actors, the other provinces of the region comprising of Barh-el-Gazal and Kanem, and the remote northern province. The absence of livelihood opportunities, food (in)security, growing impact of climate change, presence of non-state armed groups and the resultant unexploded ordinances, and lack of access to basic social services render the lives of the population in the region extremely vulnerable to forced migration, with women and youth finding themselves in aggravated precarious situations. Therefore, the project provides a multisectoral approach to this crisis, with the aim to strengthen community stabilization in the provinces of Barh-el-Gazal and Kanem by: Strengthening support to communities in addressing root causes of instability through provision of alternative and innovative means of livelihood, and implementing community-based and community-led projects; Training government and traditional authorities in human-rights based approaches to facilitate safe, orderly and secure migration and community management; Providing psychosocial and mental health support to communities in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
